    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136-a1-a34">

                <pb facs="0481" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg423"/>

                <head>Major General Sheridan to General Grant</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Headqiarters Department of the
                                Gulf</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">New Orleans</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 1, 1866—10 a. m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">General</hi>: I have an opportunity to go over to the
                    Rio Grande this evening, and by going I can settle the Ortega affair, also the
                    Sedgwick trouble, if any has occurred, and put things on a good footing, but I
                    would like to have your approval of my absence. Affairs are in good condition
                    here, and General Forsyth communicates to me from Texas frontier, no Indian
                    troubles.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">P. H. SHERIDAN, <hi rendition="#italic">Major
                    General</hi>.</p>
                <p>General U. S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant</hi>.</p>
                <p>Official:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. K. LEET, <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Adjutant
                        General</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
